{"availability":"available","full":"OceanDataTools/openvdm","name":"openvdm","description":"A comprehensive data management platform that allows vessel operators to retrieve and organizing data files created by multiple data acquisition systems into a unified cruise data package.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":15,"forks":6,"created":"2021-02-13T15:15:39Z","updated":"2026-10-11T07:22:06Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["data-management","vessel-operators"],"demo":"http://openvdm.oceandatatools.org/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:09.374Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:09.374Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:09.374Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:09.374Z","stars":15,"forks":6}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["OpenVDM is a ship-wide data management platform. It is comprised of a suite of programs and an accompanying web-application that provides vessel operators with a unified at-sea solution for retrieving and organizing files from multiple data acquisition systems into a unified cruise data package. Once the files are within the cruise data package they are immediately and safely accessible by crew and scientists. In addition OpenVDM can perform regularly backups of the cruise data package to one or more backup storage location/devices such as NAS arrays, external hard drives and even to…","OpenVDM includes a plugin architecture whereby vessel operators can develop and install their own data processing plugins used to web-based visualizations, perform data quality assurance (QA) tests and collecting data statistics at the file-level. In practice the output data from plugins is 5% the size of the raw data files, making the architecture ideal for projecting situatitional off-ship to institute or cloud-based servers over low-bandwidth connections.","OpenVDM includes a hooks architure whereby vessel operators can link custom processes to run at key milestones during a cruise such as the start/end of a cruise, after a specific data transfer or after a data processing plugin completes. The allow vessels operators to design and deploy potentially very sophisticated and asynchronous data processing workflows."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/OceanDataTools/openvdm/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"3dfba47c34fdd40e57e107494db204b2e38b6dc15599ebe4172db73a094426d4","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:09.447Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:09.447Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"OpenVDM is a ship-wide data management platform. It is comprised of a suite of programs and an accompanying web-application that provides vessel operators with a unified at-sea solution for retrieving and organizing files from multiple data acquisition systems into a unified cruise data package. Once the files are within the cruise data package they are immediately and safely accessible by crew and scientists. In addition OpenVDM can perform regularly backups of the cruise data package to one or more backup storage location/devices such as NAS arrays, external hard drives and even to…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/OceanDataTools/openvdm/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"OpenVDM includes a plugin architecture whereby vessel operators can develop and install their own data processing plugins used to web-based visualizations, perform data quality assurance (QA) tests and collecting data statistics at the file-level. In practice the output data from plugins is 5% the size of the raw data files, making the architecture ideal for projecting…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/OceanDataTools/openvdm/blob/master/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"3dfba47c34fdd40e57e107494db204b2e38b6dc15599ebe4172db73a094426d4","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/OceanDataTools/openvdm/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:09.447Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-11T07: